Without the JIT compiler (every CPU but x86: configure.ac builds it only
for __i386__/__x86_64__), a configuration with "jit_compiler = 1" still
marked the JIT as wanted: main.c set g_fs_uae_jit_compiler, so board RAM
was reserved as "32-bit memory" for a JIT that does not exist, and
config.c set cachesize 8192, which main.cpp then reset to 0 without a
word.  Now such a build ignores jit_compiler, says so on screen and runs
the interpreter; the configuration itself stays as it is, so the same
files work on x86 (with JIT) and on SPARC, ARM, PowerPC (without).
Builds with JIT compile exactly the same code as before.

Upstream: not yet sent (FrodeSolheim/fs-uae).

--- fs-uae-3.2.35/src/fs-uae/main.c	2026-11-23 22:11:40.091614400 +0100
